1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,155
Start in Core on the Calls dashboard.

2
00:00:02,335 --> 00:00:05,471
Open Archived Calls, then choose Add Archived Call.

3
00:00:05,651 --> 00:00:08,979
This is where you can enter an incident that has already happened.

4
00:00:09,299 --> 00:00:12,541
Give the call a name that will make it easy to find later.

5
00:00:12,721 --> 00:00:16,007
This exercise is a completed station inspection.

6
00:00:16,327 --> 00:00:17,969
Open the Timestamp picker.

7
00:00:18,149 --> 00:00:22,309
Choose the date of the original incident in the department’s time zone.

8
00:00:22,629 --> 00:00:24,165
Pick the original time.

9
00:00:24,345 --> 00:00:28,804
Here, the inspection was on November fourth at two fifteen in the afternoon.

10
00:00:28,984 --> 00:00:33,443
Check the timestamp before moving on, and choose the call type and priority.

11
00:00:33,763 --> 00:00:36,600
Use Nature of the Call to explain what happened.

12
00:00:36,780 --> 00:00:42,604
Keep the description brief and specific, so the next dispatcher understands why the record exists.

13
00:00:42,924 --> 00:00:44,311
Enter the location.

14
00:00:44,491 --> 00:00:48,736
If you have coordinates, check the latitude and longitude before you save.

15
00:00:48,916 --> 00:00:50,708
This is a fictional training site.

16
00:00:51,028 --> 00:00:54,975
At the bottom, choose the completion type and enter the closeout notes.

17
00:00:55,155 --> 00:00:58,931
For this exercise, leave Regenerate Call Numbers unchecked.

18
00:00:59,111 --> 00:01:01,095
Choose Add Archived Call to save.

19
00:01:01,415 --> 00:01:03,569
Search the archive for the name you entered.

20
00:01:03,749 --> 00:01:08,336
Confirm the status is Closed and the timestamp matches the original time.

21
00:01:08,656 --> 00:01:11,173
Open the record to verify the details.

22
00:01:11,353 --> 00:01:14,127
Logged On is the historical incident time.

23
00:01:14,307 --> 00:01:17,443
Closed On shows when the archive entry was completed.

24
00:01:17,763 --> 00:01:20,621
Now open Archived Calls in Omni Dispatch.

25
00:01:20,941 --> 00:01:22,435
Search for the same name.

26
00:01:22,615 --> 00:01:28,865
Check that Logged On still says two fifteen in the afternoon, and that Closed On matches the closeout in Core.

27
00:01:29,045 --> 00:01:37,515
Use the same process to document a completed security patrol or a search and rescue assignment that needs to be logged after the fact.
